    {
      "text": "On calibrated representations and the Plancherel Theorem f or affine Hecke algebras James Parkinson ∗ — This paper has two main purposes.\n\n**On calibrated representations and the Plancherel Theorem f or affine Hecke algebras James Parkinson ∗**\n\n*November 28, 2013*\n\n34 pp, 9 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** This paper has two main purposes. Firstly we generalise Ram’s combina torial construc- tion [23] of calibrated representations of the aﬃne Hecke algebra t o the multi-parameter case (including the non-reduced BCn case). We then derive the Plancherel formulae for all rank 1 and rank 2 aﬃne Hecke algebras, using our calibrated repres entations to construct all representations involved.\n\n**Outline.** 1.1 Root systems and Weyl groups; 1.2 Parameter systems; 2.1 Principal series representations; 2.2 A combinatorial construction of irreducibl; 2.3 Examples; 2.4 Characters; 3 The Plancherel Theorem; 3.1 The rank 1 algebras; A Constants and c-functions",
